# Rover on a Cube Orange+: a forward lidar, an Intel RealSense D455 depth
# camera, an aft lidar, a camera on a trigger, a 20 Ah pack. SITL backends of
# each sensor.
# Rangefinders 1, 2 and 4 look forward: the D455's 87 degrees in three columns
# of 29 (centre, left, right), the forward lidar in the centre one. ArduPilot
# files each at the 45-degree sector it faces. 3 is the aft lidar. The D455
# sees 16 m at most.
RNGFND1_TYPE 100
RNGFND1_ORIENT 0
RNGFND1_MIN 0.3
RNGFND1_MAX 16
RNGFND2_TYPE 100
RNGFND2_ORIENT 7
RNGFND2_MIN 0.3
RNGFND2_MAX 16
RNGFND3_TYPE 100
RNGFND3_ORIENT 4
RNGFND3_MIN 0.2
RNGFND3_MAX 40
RNGFND4_TYPE 100
RNGFND4_ORIENT 1
RNGFND4_MIN 0.3
RNGFND4_MAX 16
# Obstacle avoidance from those rangefinders, for a car of 3.6 x 1.8 m at
# 4 m/s on lanes the routes keep 1.5 m clear of what the map knows:
# AVOID: slow down and stop 2 m short of what is ahead (fence and proximity).
# OA (BendyRuler): steer round what is within 15 m ahead, about what the D455
# sees well, keeping 2.5 m from it: half the car's width and 1.6 m to spare; a
# wider margin would swerve from every stack beside a lane. In gz, round a box,
# the rover swung 6.5 to 12 m off the route with a lookahead of 8, 10 or 15 m
# alike, so it keeps ArduPilot's default.
PRX1_TYPE 4
AVOID_ENABLE 3
AVOID_MARGIN 2
OA_TYPE 1
OA_BR_LOOKAHEAD 15
OA_MARGIN_MAX 2.5
CAM1_TYPE 1
SERVO9_FUNCTION 10
BATT_CAPACITY 20000
